{title: More and More}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 144}

Verse 1
[D]O Lord, my God, in you [G]alone I trust,
[D/F#]For you [Em7]have been my refuge [Bm7]all my days.
[D]And even though the Enemy [G]will come,
[D/F#]You rescue [Em7]me and comfort [Bm7]me always.
Who [A/C#]is [D]like [D/F#add2]our God?

Chorus
[Gadd2]As for [G]me, I will always [D]hope in You.
I will lift [Bm7]my praise to You, more and more.
[A]As for [G]me, I will shout [D]with joy to You.
As I sing [Bm7]my praise to You, more and more.

Verse 2
My lips will tell Your deeds so marvelous,
Your power and righteousness and Yours alone.
Your mighty works I'll share with those to come,
[D]Though I may not know how to share them all.

Chorus
As for me, I will always hope in You.
I will lift my praise to You, more [Gmaj7]and more.
As for me, I [Bm]will shout with joy to You.
As I sing my praise to You, more and more.

Verse 3
Though I've seen troubles, many and bitter,
You will restore [D]my life again.
In all my struggles, [Gmaj7]You have delivered,
[Bm]You will restore my [Asus]life again.
[D]Though I've seen troubles, [Gmaj7]many and bitter,
[Bm]You will restore my [Asus]life again.
[D]In all my struggles, [Em9]You have delivered,
[Bm/F#]You will restore my life again,
[G]And again!

Chorus
[A]As for [G]me, I will always [D]hope in You.
I will lift [Bm]my praise to You, more and more.
[A]As for [G]me, I will shout [D]with joy to You.
As I sing [Bm]my praise to You, more and more.

Verse 4
Who is like our God?
